# Local scratch output
prints/

# A stray SQLite file lands here when something is run from the package directory rather than
# from `hub/`. The real database is `hub/data/`, ignored above; this one is always an accident.
hub/hub/data/*.db
hub/agentweave.db
# The driver writes this while the agent it launched is committing, so a tracked one guarantees a
# dirty tree at every iteration boundary. Globbed because a checkout running more than one daily
# window gives each window its own log.
.claude/autonomous/driver*.log

# The branch lock, for exactly the reason stated above it. `last_heartbeat` used to live inside the
# tracked STATE-<window>.json, so claiming and releasing the branch dirtied the tree and therefore
# had to be committed -- 86 of the 173 commits between 2026-09-01 and 2026-09-03 were that protocol
# talking to itself, and the log a fresh window has to read was mostly the loop breathing. The lock
# never needed to be in git: run-iteration.ps1 reads it off the disk of the machine it runs on, and
# a lock shared through a remote would be wrong anyway. One file per window.
.claude/autonomous/.heartbeat*

# Working files for the autonomous loop's own API-driving (request/response bodies), not
# durable output - the findings/log files next to it are.
.claude/autonomous/scratch/

# Staging output from scripts/migrate_openspec_corpus.py — derived, regenerate with --out
.migration/
